course: dictionary
lesson: 6991
title: A name on the map
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words are names of places, like London or Papua. This kind of word is called a proper noun, and it always starts with a capital letter. Papua is a place name, not an ordinary word for a thing.
explain: «A frog from Papua New Guinea about seven millimetres long is one of the smallest animals with a backbone.» The capital letters show that Papua New Guinea is a name. The other words, frog and animals, tell you the sentence is about living things, and the place is where the frog lives.
explain: Papua is part of two names. On its own, Papua is a large area in the western half of the island of New Guinea, and it is now part of Indonesia. Papua New Guinea is a country on the eastern half of the same island, north of Australia.
explain: When you meet a place name, use a map to check where it is. Look at the sentence too: if it talks about a country, a region or a journey, the name is probably a place.
fact: Papua is a proper noun: the name of a place, so it starts with a capital letter.
fact: Papua is a large area in the western half of the island of New Guinea, now part of Indonesia.
fact: Papua New Guinea is a country on the eastern half of the same island, north of Australia.
fact: Papua New Guinea has more than 800 languages, rainforests, mountains and birds of paradise.
fact: «Some of the smallest frogs, from Papua New Guinea and Brazil, are less than 8 millimetres long.»
exercise: What kind of word is Papua? | A verb, an action word | A plural noun, more than one thing | An adjective, a describing word | *A proper noun, the name of a place
exercise: «A frog from Papua New Guinea about seven millimetres long is one of the smallest animals with a backbone.» Which clue shows that Papua New Guinea is a name? | *Its capital letters at the start | seven | frog | animals
exercise: Papua New Guinea is on which part of the island of New Guinea? | The western half | The whole island, all of it | *The eastern half | The middle strip only
test: Which country is north of Australia? | Brazil | New Zealand | Papua | *Papua New Guinea
test: «Some of the smallest frogs, from Papua New Guinea and Brazil, are less than 8 millimetres long.» How long are these frogs? | About the length of a bus | Exactly 20 centimetres | About a metre | *Less than 8 millimetres
exam: Which sentence is true? | *Papua is now part of Indonesia | Papua is a verb meaning to jump | Papua New Guinea is in Brazil | Papua New Guinea is on the western half of New Guinea
